{"nodes": [{"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "label": "Phase 3b - Auth + Role Gate", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not the current phase. Its per-role page inventory blocker no longer exists; everything else - the literal /portal segment, the fail-closed matcher, RLS, the next= guard, the (public) migration - still applies."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_portal_route_group_collision", "label": "(portal) Route Group URL Collision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified against this repo 2026-07-22, not assumed. Parenthesised segments scope layouts but contribute nothing to the URL, so a probe at (portal)/accreditations/page.tsx fails the dev server with HTTP 500: 'You cannot have two parallel pages that resolve to the same path.' /accreditations, /calendar and /campuses are all names both sides want."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_literal_portal_segment", "label": "Decision: a Literal /portal Segment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(public) stays a route group because it only needs a shared layout; portal is a literal segment because it needs a shared namespace."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_middleware_matcher", "label": "Fail-Closed Middleware Matcher", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "matcher: [\"/portal/:path*\"] is one rule, fail-closed - any route added under /portal is protected the moment the file exists. Enumerating bare paths fails open: the day someone adds /reports and forgets the matcher entry, that page is public."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_rls_boundary", "label": "RLS Is the Authorization Boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:127", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Middleware only redirects unauthenticated visitors; it cannot answer whether this representative may read program 999. A user requesting a record they do not own must get zero rows from RLS and a 404, never a middleware pass over a populated page."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_service_role_bypass", "label": "A Service-Role Query Is a Full RLS Bypass", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:136", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Server Components and Route Handlers must query through the user's session client, not the service-role key."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_app_metadata_role_claim", "label": "Role Claim Belongs in app_metadata", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:163", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never user_metadata, which users can edit themselves - that is a privilege-escalation path."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_next_open_redirect_guard", "label": "next= Open-Redirect Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:143", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deep links survive auth via ?next=, defaulting to /portal, but next must be validated as a relative path beginning with /portal or it is an open redirect."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_role_dispatcher", "label": "/portal Is the Role Dispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:145", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No separate /portal/dashboard; /portal itself dispatches on the role claim."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_shared_url_rule", "label": "Shared URL vs Role-Prefixed URL Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If two roles can open the same database row it gets one URL and the role decides what renders; a feature for exactly one role gets a role-prefixed URL. Two stack-specific reasons to resist role-prefixed URLs for shared records: nodemailer notifications would have to resolve the recipient's role to build a link, and pdf-lib document UUIDs need a stable resolution target."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_render_split_not_route_split", "label": "Per-Role Views Are a Rendering Split, Not a Routing Split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:115", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Different pages per role' most often means different views and actions over shared objects. Only split the route when the underlying data is genuinely disjoint."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_no_workflow_state_in_path", "label": "Do Not Encode Workflow State in the Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/portal/accreditations/[id]/pending-review rots the moment the record transitions. Keep the bare id and render from the state persisted in Postgres."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_public_migration", "label": "(public) Route Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:147", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One atomic change: move the flat public routes into (public)/, move Navbar + Footer out of the root layout, leave login/ where it is, and confirm every public URL is byte-identical afterwards."}, {"id": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_dual_role_question", "label": "Can One Person Hold Two Roles?", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:187", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If yes, the role dispatcher needs a role switcher and role-prefixed URLs become actively harmful. Also changes whether role is a column or a join table, and every RLS policy after it."}], "edges": [{"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_portal_route_group_collision", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_literal_portal_segment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_middleware_matcher", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_rls_boundary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_service_role_bypass", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_app_metadata_role_claim", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_next_open_redirect_guard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_role_dispatcher", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_shared_url_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md", "source_location": "plans/03-auth-role-gate.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_phase", "target": "plans_03_auth_role_gate_no_workflow_state_in_path", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/0